AUDIO: 'Apple\'s about to change how a lot of people pay for their hardware, and it might be happening next week. According to Bloomberg\'s Mark Gurman, Apple is partnering with Klarna on a new program called the Apple Upgrade Program, launching in the US on Tuesday, July 28th. And it\'s a little bit bigger in'

[00:13] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'scope. So, here\'s how it works. Apple Upgrade lets you finance an iPhone, an iPad, a Mac, and Apple Watch models. iPhone and Apple Watch is get a 24-month term. iPads and Macs get 36-month terms. During that term, you can pay the device'

[00:27] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'off early if you want to, upgrade early to something newer, or just keep the device only once it\'s paid fully off. So, it\'s a lease that ends in ownership. Just pretty standard stuff. If you wanted to, which is basically the same'

